# Extra glslc flags for this repo's shaders. Read by cbuild --vulkan
# (/home/coopa/.sww/packages/cbuild/cbuild). One token per line.
#
# Lets toyengine's shaders #include <gfx/...> headers from gfxcoopa's shared
# base shader library instead of keeping local copies.
#
# Path is RELATIVE to the repo root -- cbuild invokes glslc with cwd=repo root.
# Not ${SIBLINGS}: cbuild hardcodes that to the parent of this checkout
# (os.path.dirname(os.getcwd())), which points outside the repo now that the
# coopa libraries are vendored as submodules under libs/.
#
# The CMake build does NOT read this file: gfx_add_shader_target() adds
# gfxcoopa's assets/shaders to -I on its own, derived from the location of the
# GfxShaders.cmake it included (see gfxcoopa/cmake/GfxShaders.cmake), so that
# path follows the submodule automatically.
# ORDER MATTERS, and matches gfx_add_shader_target() exactly (see
# gfxcoopa/cmake/GfxShaders.cmake:81-82): this repo's OWN shader dir first, then
# gfxcoopa's base library. glslc searches -I in order, so a gfx/ header present
# in both resolves to toyengine's copy -- consumers shadow the base library.
#
# The second entry is new. CMake always passed it (INCLUDE_DIR defaults to
# SHADER_DIR) but cbuild only ever got the gfxcoopa -I, so `cbuild --vulkan`
# failed on shadow_cube.frag/.vert -- whose gfx/surface/shadow_cube_fs.glsl
# exists only here -- while the CMake build compiled them fine. Unrelated to the
# libs/ move: the same gap existed with the old ${SIBLINGS} path.
-I
assets/shaders
-I
libs/gfxcoopa/assets/shaders
